<newsitem itemid="106592" id="root" date="1996-10-09" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: BNB Resources H1 pretax profit rises 33 pct.</title>
<headline>BNB Resources H1 pretax profit rises 33 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.9		    vs 5.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.4		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.35		   vs 1.77</p>
<p> Turnover		   56.3		   vs 48.8</p>
<p> Operating result	 2.40		   vs 1.80</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.05		   vs 0.03</p>
<p> Tax			  0.82		   vs 0.62</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.53		   vs 1.15</p>
<p> Attributable	     1.48		   vs 1.15</p>
<p> Pay date		   n/a</p>
<p> Div registration date  n/a</p>
<p> Ex-div date		n/a</p>
<p>NOTE- Recruitment, training and communications group BNB Resources Plc said in its results statement it had confidence for the longer term &quot;because of the improved balance of its profits, the quality of its businesses and the overall market outlook.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
